                <pb facs="0687" n="615" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg615"/>

                <head>Italian Industrial Society of Constantinople</head>
                <note rend="inline" rendition="#center" type="source">[Translation.]</note>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Italian Industrial Society of Constantinople</hi>, <lb/>
                    <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-29">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 29, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The tragical death of President Lincoln,
                    lately snatched from the presipency of the great American republic, is a loss to
                    be deplored by universal humanity.</p>
                <p>Under this impression the Italian Industrial Society of Constantinople, of both
                    the male and female sections, hasten to bear their tribute of grief for this
                    deplorable event to your excellency.</p>
                <p>We beg your excellency to accept this tribute of sorrow as a proof of that
                    fraternity which at no distant day will unite in sympathy the people of both
                    hemispheres, and we humbly request that you will do us the honor to transmit
                    this letter to the government at Washington.</p>
                <p>Accept, excellency, our most cordial salutations.</p>
                <p>For the society:</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GUISEPPE DE ANDREA,</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice-President</hi>. <lb/>
                    <signed>PIETRO TABBUCA, </signed>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary</hi>. </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Joy Morris</hi>, <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">United States Minister at Constantinople</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
